==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂en-}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}}
From {{uder|en|la|ambiguus||moving from side to side, of doubtful nature}}, from {{m|la|ambigere||to go about, wander, doubt}}, from {{m|la|ambi-||around, about, on both sides}} + {{m|la|agere||to drive, move}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ambiguous.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Open to multiple [[interpretation]]s.
#: {{syn|en|equivocal|unclear}}
#: {{ant|en|unambiguous|clear}}
#: {{ux|en|The politician was criticized for his '''ambiguous''' statements and lack of precision.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|of persons}} [[hesitant|Hesitant]]; uncertain; not taking sides.
#* '''1662''' {{w|Thomas Salusbury}}
#*: And forasmuch as in this same question I am '''ambiguous''', and Simplicius is resolute....

